  CVE-2026-35538|2026-04-03T05:16:21.647|2026-04-03T05:16:21.647|3.1|LOW|CWE-88|N/A|false|An issue was discovered in Roundcube Webmail before 1.5.14 and 1.6.14. Unsanitized IMAP SEARCH command arguments could lead to IMAP injection or CSRF bypass during mail search.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35538|0.00000|0.00000|2.1700
  CVE-2026-35537|2026-04-03T04:17:10.313|2026-04-03T04:17:10.313|3.7|LOW|CWE-502|N/A|false|An issue was discovered in Roundcube Webmail before 1.5.14 and 1.6.14. Unsafe deserialization in the redis/memcache session handler may lead to arbitrary file write operations by unauthenticated attackers via crafted session data.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35537|0.00000|0.00000|2.5900
