  CVE-2026-28815|2026-04-03T03:16:18.093|2026-04-03T03:16:18.093|0.0|NONE|N/A|N/A|false|A remote attacker can supply a short X-Wing HPKE encapsulated key and trigger an out-of-bounds read in the C decapsulation path, potentially causing a crash or memory disclosure depending on runtime protections. This issue is fixed in swift-crypto version 4.3.1.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-28815|0.00000|0.00000|0.0000
