  CVE-2022-4986|2026-04-02T22:16:23.597|2026-04-02T23:17:03.697|8.7|HIGH|CWE-400|N/A|false|Hirschmann EagleSDV version 05.4.01 prior to 05.4.02 contains a denial-of-service vulnerability that causes the device to crash during session establishment when using TLS 1.0 or TLS 1.1. Attackers can trigger a crash by initiating TLS connections with these protocol versions to disrupt service availability.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-4986|0.00000|0.00000|6.0900
